id: E777
draft: true
contributor_id: 2501
trigger_tool: conan|source|review
phase: source-acquisition|validation
error_signature: historical source_url owner differs from official current release owner
severity: 2
category: source-identity, release, conan
match_keywords: upstream transfer, release owner, historical archive, official tag, source SHA256, Conan source
title: Revalidate official source owner and archive hash for each new upstream version
root_cause: A historical recipe records the owner and URL of its own released tag, not an immutable owner for all future versions. Replacing only the version in that URL can target a stale repository path and leave the new source identity unproven.
affected_scope: Libraries with changed upstream repository ownership or release location when adapting a version newer than an existing archive.
verification_cmd: Compare historical source_url with the current official release tag and homepage, download the versioned archive, check its SHA256, then bind that exact archive and hash to the target Conan create log.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: per-version-official-release-identity
rec_description: Resolve the maintainer's current release page and tag for the requested version, pin its official archive URL and SHA256 in conandata, and use a byte-identical local source archive for target-only offline validation without changing the checked-in URL.
rec_command: Inspect release tag and historical manifest; compute SHA256 of the official tarball; verify the W3 bundle hash and Conan source log before reporting build success.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe-and-evidence
forbid_1_pattern: replace.*version.*historical.*source_url
forbid_1_reason: The old owner and URL are version-specific evidence, not a valid source location for every later tag.
forbid_1_consequence: A redirected, missing, or unintended archive may be downloaded while the recipe still appears plausible.
principles: []
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [DRAFT-monocypher-4.0.2-release-vs-tag-archive]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
